# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# 99-rocket-npu-pm.rules — let an unprivileged NPU process drive the RK3576 power cycle.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. On the RK3576 a job whose DPU output element is wider than one byte
# (any fp16 convolution, either int32 matmul writer) leaves the NEXT submit completing
# normally and writing nothing. What clears it is the runtime-PM autosuspend cycling the
# NPU power domain, not elapsed time — so the library has to wait for that cycle before
# the next submit, and mainline sizes the autosuspend delay at 50 ms for a display
# pipeline. Waiting out that timer costs ~105 ms per call.
#
# Instead the library DRIVES the transition: write a zero delay, wait for the device to
# report `suspended`, put the original delay back. That costs one real power cycle
# (224x224 k3 s2 at fp16: 13.75 ms against 226) and leaves the steady-state policy every
# other consumer of the NPU sees unchanged.
#
# It needs write access to `power/autosuspend_delay_ms`, which is root-only by default.
# This rule hands that one file to the `render` group — the same group that already owns
# `/dev/accel/accel0`, so it grants nothing to anyone who could not already submit NPU
# work. Without it the library falls back to the plain idle and simply pays the timer.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -m 0644 udev/99-rocket-npu-pm.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload && sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=platform
#
# Verify (as an unprivileged user in `render`):
#   test -w /sys/bus/platform/devices/27700000.npu/power/autosuspend_delay_ms && echo ok
#
# Turn the behaviour off at runtime regardless: ROCKET_RK3576_PM_KICK=0.
#
# LOWERING THE DELAY OUTRIGHT IS THE OTHER OPTION AND IT IS NOT FREE. A resume costs
# about 230 us, and a lower delay makes every job whose inter-job gap falls between the
# new delay and the old one pay it — at a 16.7 ms gap, one 60 Hz frame, a submit goes
# from 1124 us to 1372. Prefer this rule; reach for a lower delay only on a box whose NPU
# work is the only thing that matters.

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVERS=="rocket", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'chgrp render $sys$devpath/power/autosuspend_delay_ms 2>/dev/null; chmod g+w $sys$devpath/power/autosuspend_delay_ms 2>/dev/null'"
